I love crash team racing it was one of  my favorite games growing up and it  still is to this day I remember every  level every item and every shortcut from  the original and even now I can pick it  up and still compete with some of my  best lap times if the devil himself came  up to me and said Nick I want that soul  of yours but you can keep it if you beat  me in a game of your choosing there's a  good chance I'd dig up a ps1 and pass  them a controller I still fervently  believe that with its drift and  powerslide mechanics alone  it is hands-down the best kart racer of  all time and that's before we toss in  classic characters and levels like dr.  engine and pop experiment so when I saw  an opportunity to jump in and play the  remake I had to see if he was shaping up  to my very high standards of what I  wanted to be thankfully I can say with  about 90% of surety that I have nothing  to worry about  first off presentation wise it's  incredible the three tracks I was able  to play crash Cove polar pass and dingo  Canyon look great there's so much added  detail they packed into every nook and  cranny not only on the track itself but  particularly in the background  polar bears climbing along banners a  train chugging along just above the  track I was so focused on the race that  it wasn't until I looked over at the  screen of the player next to me that I  realized just how much extra there is  going on off the main course  each character also now has their own  set of animations for jumping or  celebrating they've rerecorded many of  my favorite characters exclamation and  taunts while also adding new ones that  fit each personality cortex for example  has never seen more like a bumbling  maniacal mad scientist and he does here  not only that explosions from bombs or  missiles whisk by my ears as I sped past  competitor potions I threw ahead landed  with a satisfying splash on top of  another racer and of course hearing the  re-recorded title theme music playing  through the headphones before I put them  on brought back a potent wave of  nostalgia  [Music]  I was able to speak with the lead  developer who was there to talk a bit  about our experiences with the game when  we were younger I asked him what his  favorite track was they were looking at  speedrunners to balance any of the  characters or shortcuts and if battle  mode was coming back among other things  for the record it was hotter skyway yes  they're removing some of the shortcuts  you can access by going out of bounds  but plan on keeping everything that was  designed as intentional and yes battle  mode will return when I asked if they  were considering adding and no items  variant of races for online he said that  they're still evaluating their options  in terms of new modes he genuinely  seemed just as big of a fan of the  originals me he said that they're trying  their very best to make it control  exactly like I remember and then  ultimately they will have accomplished  their goal if our lap times and time  trial are the same as they were in the  original as for replicating that feel  for the most part I think they've  succeeded from the moment I picked up  the controller I was tapping X to charge  up my initial boost out of the gate and  immediately went into lining up my angle  to get the perfect power slide around  the corner it plays just like it used to  you start sliding you charge your turbo  and hit l1 to boost up to three times  the longer you let it charge the longer  your boost lasts however it feels like  they shorten the length of time that  boosts lasts with it particularly being  noticeable on long straight lanes  without turns on crash Cove for example  after boosting into the final stretch  used to be very easy to keep your boost  going through using the turbo pads up to  the finish line but in nitro fueled I  fell a little short of that coming out  of your drift also felt just the tiniest  bit off as well I wasn't able to narrow  down what it was until I went home that  night and played the original again I  think they adjusted your turning radius  after boosting whether it's how far you  turn or how quickly you turn I'm not  positive yet but it led to a couple  cases where I accidentally boosted off  the ledge or into a wall because my  angle was off  that said I could be wrong I hadn't  played the original in a few years so I  may have just been rusty I only played  for 45 minutes and if anything it's  still an early build so there's always  room to fine-tune everything  worst case scenario it just means that I  need to slightly adjust how I approach  those turns  nitro fueled still vastly exceeded my  expectations and I can't wait to pick it  up and feel that rush of competition  again one of the games I play better  than anyone I know  however if nitrous oxide is still a  dirty cheater after all these years I'm  going to lose it  [Music]
 

